      "message": "fix(verify): a tilted plane reads its stock cap in its own frame\n\nThe tilted verify branch started its local stock cap at the world stock\ntop minus the plane origin's Z, and only raised it with the projected\nbox corners. On a side plane (A +90 / A -90) of a 60 x 60 x 70 blank the\ncap stayed at 70, not the real 30. A shank 11 mm over the side face was\nnamed a ShankHit, and a clearance 10 mm over it FirstTraverseLow and\nRapidInStock. The cap is now the projected corners' maximum only. The\ncorner projection still over-reports, so a real collision convicts.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/tilt_stock_cap.rs (A +90 and A -90).\n\nFixes #3004\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
